'''Juan Alberto''' "'''Juancho'''" '''Hernangómez Geuer''' (born 28 September 1995) is a Spanish professional [[basketball]] player for [[Panathinaikos B.C.|Panathinaikos]] of the [[Greek Basketball League]] (GBL) and the [[EuroLeague]]. He was selected by the [[Denver Nuggets]] with the 15th overall pick in the [[2016 NBA Draft|2016 NBA draft]] and spent seven seasons in the [[National Basketball Association|NBA]] before returning to [[Europe]]. He is an [[All-EuroLeague Team|All-EuroLeague Second Team]] selection and won the EuroLeague in [[2023–24 EuroLeague|2024]].

Hernangómez represents the senior [[Spain men's national basketball team|Spanish national team]] in international competition.<ref name="RealGM">{{cite web |url=http://basketball.realgm.com/player/Juan-Alberto-Hernangomez/Summary/52816 |title=Juancho Hernangomez Player Profile |work=RealGM.com |access-date=9 March 2016}}</ref> He won the [[2019 FIBA Basketball World Cup]] and played a crucial part in winning the [[EuroBasket 2022]], scoring a game-high 27 points in the final against France.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://nba.nbcsports.com/2022/09/18/behind-27-from-juancho-hernangomez-spain-knocks-off-france-to-win-eurobasket-title/ |title=Behind 27 from Juancho Hernangomez, Spain knocks off France to win EuroBasket title |date=18 September 2022}}</ref> Additionally to his playing career, Hernangómez co-starred in the [[Netflix]] basketball film ''[[Hustle (2022 film)|Hustle]]'' in 2022, alongside [[Adam Sandler]].
